WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.508 --> 00:00:03.341
(xylophone music)

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.950
- [Luca] I build models
sometimes with weird materials.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.690
I've always found aviation
to just be really kind

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.023
of magical just because airplanes
are engineering marvels.

00:00:17.932 --> 00:00:19.860
And I wanted to marry that

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.113
with the unconventional
building technique.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.470
- [Announcer] This Great
Big Story was made possible

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.060
by Geico.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:27.893
Believe it.

00:00:27.893 --> 00:00:31.431
Geico could save you 15%
or more on car insurance.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.264
(xylophone music)

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:42.370
- [Luca] For my day job I
work in IT and management.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.020
but I've just always
been creatively-minded.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.762
I've always been drawn to
those kinds of projects.

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:52.600
I've been making things
since I could figure out

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.010
what tape and string were.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:55.910
I was super young.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.400
I probably drove my parents crazy.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.010
I'm best known for the paper
airplane models that I make.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.700
What I use to build the
models is manila folder,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:06.533
glue,

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.366
an X-ACTO,

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:09.610
and a straight edge, essentially.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:12.730
It's hard to know exactly how
many folders I've gone through

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.410
but I would say it's in the
hundreds for this project,

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.593
and there's a lot of scrap left over.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:21.530
I kept it to a minimal set of materials

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.990
just because I like the
challenge of building something

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.930
from only one thing and
having to figure out how

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:29.413
to make that serve many purposes.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.460
The model began on a
much less detailed scale.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.380
But I did, over time, realize

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:42.890
that I could start building in more.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.050
Articulating functions,

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.720
more details in the interior.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.240
And inside there are
tissues in the bathroom.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.100
There are lights on the seats.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.651
Nothing actually moves in the cabin

00:01:51.651 --> 00:01:54.083
but all the detail is there.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.580
I've always just found the triple seven

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.330
to be a really elegant,

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.730
nicely proportioned plane.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:03.450
And so it was partly
an issue of aesthetics.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.283
I've always just been a fan
of that particular model.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.860
I studied pictures online.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.082
Some technical drawings.

00:02:11.082 --> 00:02:12.940
I actually create my own plans,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.080
and there's just no
guide for how to do that,

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.580
so I'm basically learning along the way.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.060
It's simultaneously kind of freeing

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:23.910
and also really frustrating
not to have plans.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.830
I can really take it in any direction.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.720
But you have to be
incredibly inventive about

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.143
how you solve problems because
it really hasn't been done.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.550
A lot of people probably
think that my end game

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.530
was absolute perfection with the model,

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.750
but in fact it was more just
about the process of making it.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.700
It's the thought of the completed product

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.480
that inspires me and just being able

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.533
to solve such a complex problem.

00:02:53.533 --> 00:02:57.500
It's just what I derive a
lot of satisfaction from.

